{
  "id": "musica_parrandera_paisa",
  "name": "Música parrandera (Antioquian December party song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Música parrandera is the festive party song of Antioquia, sung at the December holiday parrandas of Medellín and the paisa towns; it took shape in the 1950s and 1960s and was recorded on Medellín labels such as Codiscos. A guitar-and-requinto string combo with bass and guacharaca scraper backs a singer in quick, bouncy parranda and merengue rhythms, the lyrics full of double meanings and picaresque stories. The requinto card stands in for the requinto guitar and the guayo card for the guacharaca.",
  "recipe": "classic South American mid-1950s música parrandera, drinking Song, americas branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. classical nylon-string guitar, credited requinto guayo source unspecified, electric bass. live tracking. shure SM57, transformer-coupled solid-state pre, colored vintage console, optical compressor. tape 15ips spring reverb.",
